[217.772748, "o", "Error: Could not resolve dependencies for project com.google.auto:auto-common:jar:1.0-SNAPSHOT\r\n> "]
[217.772923, "o", "Specific Error: Could not find artifact com.sun:tools:jar:11.0.27 at specified path /usr/lib/jvm/java-11-openjdk-amd64/../lib/tools.jar\r\n> \r\n> "]
[217.773036, "o", "Root Cause:\r\n> -----------\r\n> "]
[217.773414, "o", "1. The project is being built with Java 11 (OpenJDK 11.0.27)\r\n> 2. The compile-testing:0.7 dependency (used in common/pom.xml as a test dependency) has a system-scoped dependency on com.sun:tools\r\n> "]
[217.773552, "o", "3. This dependency uses ${toolsjar} as the systemPath\r\n"]
[217.773603, "o", "> "]
[217.773642, "o", "4. The toolsjar property is set in profiles that activate based on file existence:\r\n"]
[217.773669, "o", "> "]
[217.773802, "o", "   - default-profile: checks for ${java.home}/../lib/tools.jar\r\n"]
[217.773829, "o", "> "]
[217.773947, "o", "   - mac-profile: checks for ${java.home}/../Classes/classes.jar\r\n> "]
[217.774112, "o", "5. In Java 9+, tools.jar was removed and its contents were moved into the JDK modules\r\n"]
[217.774141, "o", "> "]
[217.774294, "o", "6. Neither profile activates in Java 11, so ${toolsjar} is undefined\r\n"]
[217.774362, "o", "> "]
[217.774485, "o", "7. Maven tries to resolve the dependency but fails because the path is invalid\r\n"]
[217.774526, "o", "> \r\n> "]
[217.774569, "o", "Solution:"]
[217.774627, "o", "\r\n> "]
[217.774663, "o", "---------"]
[217.774696, "o", "\r\n> "]
[217.774859, "o", "Update compile-testing to version 0.10 or later which supports Java 9+ and doesn't require tools.jar."]
[217.774903, "o", "\r\n> "]
[217.775077, "o", "Alternatively, we could add a Java 9+ profile that sets toolsjar to a dummy value or excludes the dependency."]
[217.775118, "o", "\r\n> "]
[217.775155, "o", "\r\n> "]
[217.775316, "o", "The simplest fix is to update common/pom.xml to use compile-testing version 0.10 instead of 0.7."]
[217.775356, "o", "\r\n> "]
[217.77539, "o", "EOF"]
